<%#
  The wiring table (stage 3, S3-3): connections between two labelled ends, with a wire and a
  note, edited inline, in position order. Read-only rendering (`editable: false`) is what S3-4
  reuses on the public page, which is why this partial takes LOCALS rather than reading @project/
  @connections off the controller the way projects/_tasks.html.erb does -- a public-page
  controller has no reason to alias its own ivars just to satisfy this partial.

  Locals:
    project     -- the Maker::Project the composer and each row's Save/Remove post against
    connections -- every Maker::Connection on the project, in position order
                   (Maker::Project#connections' own default scope) -- ProjectsController#show
                   loads this in ONE query; this partial issues none of its own
    editable    -- true on the project page (this user's own project); false renders plain cells
                   and no composer
    layout      -- the Maker::ProjectKind::Layout the page renders from (titles, intros). A LOCAL
                   for the same reason `project` and `connections` are: this partial is the ONE
                   panel both pages render, and each holds its layout under a different name --
                   @panel_layout on the maker's page, `pub.layout` on the visitor's (2026-09-09,
                   the page editor)
  Optional (a refused row, Projects::ConnectionsController#update, 2026-11-02):
    drafts      -- { connection id => the refused Maker::Connection, typed values and all }
    row_errors  -- { connection id => the sentence it was refused with }

  A <form> CANNOT SPAN TABLE CELLS, so each row's <form> sits OUTSIDE the table -- one empty
  form_with per row (nothing inside the block but the CSRF/method-override hidden fields Rails
  always inserts) -- and every field plus the row's Save button point back at it by id via the
  HTML `form=` attribute. project_wiring_test.rb asserts that wiring directly (`input[form=?]`
  against "connection-#{id}"), not merely that the fields render.

  ONE FORM PER ROW MEANS A SAVE KEEPS ONLY ITS OWN ROW, AND THE PAGE SAYS SO (2026-11-02, the UX
  audit's C10). Saving one row reloads the page, so an edit typed into another row was lost without
  a word. `wiring_controller.js` marks a row "Unsaved" as it is edited, asks before a Save that
  would drop another row's edits, and asks before leaving the page with any. Every cell's field has
  its own label now (visually hidden: the column heading says it to the eye, the label says it to a
  screen reader, which met four unnamed inputs per row).
%>
<% drafts = local_assigns.fetch(:drafts, {}) %>
<% row_errors = local_assigns.fetch(:row_errors, {}) %>
<%# QUIET AT ZERO (stage 4, S4-1): no connections is the heading and its composer. The count span
    goes with the table it counts -- "0 connections" beside a heading is not information -- and the
    sentence that stood where the table does said no more than the empty panel already did. The
    composer is the one control an empty panel exists to offer; it sits in the head, a direct child
    of `.panel-head`, like every panel's composer (2026-11-02, the UX audit's C4). %>
<section class="panel wiring-panel<%= " panel--quiet" if connections.empty? %>" id="project-wiring"
         <%= tag.attributes(data: { controller: "wiring" }) if editable && connections.any? %>>
  <div class="panel-head">
    <h2><%= panel_title(layout, "wiring") %></h2>
    <% if connections.any? %>
      <span class="mono muted"><%= pluralize(connections.size, "connection") %></span>
    <% end %>
    <% if editable %>
      <%= render "projects/wiring_composer", project: project %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <%= panel_intro(layout, "wiring") %>

  <% if connections.any? %>
    <% if editable %>
      <% connections.each do |connection| %>
        <%= form_with model: connection, scope: :connection, url: connection_path(connection),
                      method: :patch, id: "connection-#{connection.id}",
                      data: { action: "submit->wiring#save" } do %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
    <table class="table wiring">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="col-from">From</th>
          <th class="col-to">To</th>
          <th class="col-wire">Wire</th>
          <th class="col-note">Note</th>
          <% if editable %>
            <th class="col-actions"><span class="label-hidden">Actions</span></th>
          <% end %>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% connections.each_with_index do |connection, index| %>
          <% form_id = "connection-#{connection.id}" %>
          <% shown = drafts[connection.id] || connection %>
          <%# A REFUSED ROW IS AN UNSAVED ROW: it holds what was typed and the store does not, so it
              renders already marked dirty, its "Unsaved" shown, and leaving the page asks about it
              exactly as it would have before the Save that was refused. %>
          <% refused = row_errors.key?(connection.id) %>
          <tr class="wiring-row<%= " wiring-row--refused" if refused %>"
              <%= tag.attributes(data: { wiring_target: "row", dirty: ("true" if refused) }) if editable %>>
            <% if editable %>
              <% { "from_label" => "From", "to_label" => "To", "wire" => "Wire", "note" => "Note" }.each do |field, heading| %>
                <td class="col-<%= field.delete_suffix("_label") %>">
                  <label class="label-hidden" for="<%= form_id %>-<%= field %>"><%= heading %>, connection <%= index + 1 %></label>
                  <%= text_field_tag "connection[#{field}]", shown.public_send(field),
                                     form: form_id, id: "#{form_id}-#{field}",
                                     data: { action: "input->wiring#edit" } %>
                </td>
              <% end %>
              <td class="col-actions">
                <%= submit_tag "Save", form: form_id, class: "btn small" %>
                <%= button_to "Remove", connection_path(connection), method: :delete,
                              class: "linkbtn danger small",
                              form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "Remove #{connection.from_label} → #{connection.to_label}?",
                                              action: "submit->wiring#save" } } %>
                <span class="wiring-unsaved muted" <%= "hidden" unless refused %>>Unsaved</span>
                <% if (row_error = row_errors[connection.id]) %>
                  <span class="wiring-row-error" role="alert"><%= row_error %></span>
                <% end %>
              </td>
            <% else %>
              <td class="col-from"><%= connection.from_label %></td>
              <td class="col-to"><%= connection.to_label %></td>
              <td class="col-wire"><%= connection.wire %></td>
              <td class="col-note"><%= connection.note %></td>
            <% end %>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  <% end %>
</section>
